### Ymmo API — manual test suite
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request"
### above each block. Run the seed (db/seed.sql) first so data exists.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### --- 0. Health -------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### =====================================================================
### AUTH
### =====================================================================

### 1. Register a new buyer (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.buyer@ymmo.fr",
  "password": "motdepasse123",
  "first_name": "Camille",
  "last_name": "Durand"
}

### 2. Register again with same email (expect 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.buyer@ymmo.fr",
  "password": "motdepasse123",
  "first_name": "Camille",
  "last_name": "Durand"
}

### 3. Register with invalid input (expect 400 — bad email + short password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123",
  "first_name": "X",
  "last_name": "Y"
}

### 4. Login as AGENT (captures the token for the next requests)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agent@ymmo.fr",
  "password": "agent1234"
}

### 5. Login with wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agent@ymmo.fr",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 6. Me — with the agent token (expect 200 + agent profile)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 7. Me — without a token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me

### =====================================================================
### PROPERTIES — public
### =====================================================================

### 8. List all available properties (expect 4 seeded, DRAFT hidden)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties

### 9. Filter by city
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties?city=Paris

### 10. Filter by price + sort ascending
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties?max_price=500000&sort=price_asc

### 11. Filter by sector (RESIDENTIAL only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties?sector=RESIDENTIAL

### 12. Filter by energy rating D or better
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties?max_energy=D

### 13. Pagination (2 per page, page 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties?page_size=2&page=1

### 14. Get one property by id (expect 200 + view_count increment)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1

### 15. Get a non-existing property (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/9999

### =====================================================================
### PROPERTIES — protected (staff only)
### =====================================================================

### 16. Create a property WITHOUT token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test sans token",
  "category_id": 2,
  "price": 300000,
  "area": 60,
  "city": "Nice",
  "postal_code": "06000",
  "agency_id": 1
}

### 17. Create a property AS AGENT (expect 201, status DRAFT, auto reference)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "title": "Appartement T2 rénové",
  "description": "Refait à neuf, proche commerces",
  "category_id": 2,
  "price": 295000,
  "area": 48,
  "rooms": 2,
  "bedrooms": 1,
  "energy_rating": "C",
  "city": "Nice",
  "postal_code": "06000",
  "agency_id": 1
}

### 18. Create with invalid input (expect 400 — missing title, price <= 0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "category_id": 2,
  "price": 0,
  "area": 48,
  "city": "Nice",
  "postal_code": "06000",
  "agency_id": 1
}

### 19. Update a property (expect 200 — partial update)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/2
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "price": 630000,
  "status": "AVAILABLE"
}

### 20. Delete a property (expect 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/3
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### =====================================================================
### RBAC — a BUYER must NOT manage properties
### =====================================================================

### 21. Login as BUYER
# @name loginBuyer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "buyer@ymmo.fr",
  "password": "buyer1234"
}

### 22. Buyer tries to create a property (expect 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{
  "title": "Tentative interdite",
  "category_id": 2,
  "price": 200000,
  "area": 40,
  "city": "Lille",
  "postal_code": "59000",
  "agency_id": 1
}

### =====================================================================
### FAVORITES — any authenticated user (here: the buyer)
### =====================================================================

### 23. Add a favorite WITHOUT token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/favorites

### 24. Add a favorite as buyer (expect 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/favorites
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 25. Add the SAME favorite again (idempotent, expect 204 — no duplicate error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/favorites
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 26. Favorite a non-existing property (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/9999/favorites
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 27. List my favorites (expect 200, contains property 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/favorites
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 28. Remove the favorite (expect 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/favorites
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 29. List again (expect 200, now empty)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/favorites
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### =====================================================================
### PHOTOS — staff only (use the AGENT token from request #4)
### =====================================================================

### 30. Add a photo WITHOUT token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/photos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://placehold.co/800x600", "is_primary": true }

### 31. Add a photo as BUYER (expect 403 — not staff)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/photos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "url": "https://placehold.co/800x600", "is_primary": true }

### 32. Add a photo as AGENT (expect 201) — captures the new photo id
# @name addPhoto
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/photos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "url": "https://placehold.co/800x600?text=New", "is_primary": true }

### 33. Add a photo with an invalid URL (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/photos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "url": "not-a-url" }

### 34. Add a photo to a missing property (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/9999/photos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "url": "https://placehold.co/800x600" }

### 35. Check the photo shows up on the property (expect it in "photos")
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1

### 36. Delete the photo just added as AGENT (expect 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/photos/{{addPhoto.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 37. Delete a non-existing photo (expect 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/photos/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### =====================================================================
### MESSAGING — client (buyer) <-> agent (id 1)
### =====================================================================

### 38. Login as DIRECTOR (a third party, for the access-control test)
# @name loginDirector
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "director@ymmo.fr", "password": "director1234" }

### 39. Buyer starts a conversation with the agent about property 1 (expect 201)
# @name startConv
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "agent_id": 1, "property_id": 1 }

### 40. Start the SAME conversation again (idempotent — same id, no duplicate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "agent_id": 1, "property_id": 1 }

### 41. Buyer sends a message (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations/{{startConv.response.body.id}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "body": "Bonjour, ce bien est-il toujours disponible ?" }

### 42. Send a message WITHOUT token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations/{{startConv.response.body.id}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "test" }

### 43. DIRECTOR (not a participant) tries to read the thread (expect 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations/{{startConv.response.body.id}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

### 44. Agent's unread count (expect 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 45. Agent reads the thread (marks messages as read)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations/{{startConv.response.body.id}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 46. Agent's unread count again (expect 0)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 47. Agent lists their conversations (expect the thread)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 48. Send to a non-existing conversation (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations/999999/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "body": "test" }

### =====================================================================
### VISITS — client requests, agent manages
### =====================================================================

### 49. Request a visit WITHOUT token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/visits
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scheduled_at": "2026-12-01T15:00:00Z" }

### 50. Buyer requests a visit of property 1 (expect 201) — captures the visit id
# @name requestVisit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/visits
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "scheduled_at": "2026-12-01T15:00:00Z", "notes": "Disponible l'apres-midi" }

### 51. Request a visit in the PAST (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1/visits
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "scheduled_at": "2020-01-01T10:00:00Z" }

### 52. Request a visit on a missing property (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/9999/visits
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "scheduled_at": "2026-12-01T15:00:00Z" }

### 53. Buyer lists their visits (expect the visit, status REQUESTED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visits
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 54. Agent confirms the visit (expect 200, status CONFIRMED)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visits/{{requestVisit.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "status": "CONFIRMED" }

### 55. Director (not a participant) tries to update it (expect 403)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visits/{{requestVisit.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

{ "status": "CANCELLED" }

### 56. Update with an invalid status (expect 400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visits/{{requestVisit.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "status": "BANANA" }

### =====================================================================
### MEETINGS — organizer = director, participant = agent (id 1)
### =====================================================================

### 57. Create a meeting WITHOUT token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "agency_id": 1, "title": "Reunion equipe", "start_at": "2026-12-01T09:00:00Z", "end_at": "2026-12-01T10:00:00Z" }

### 58. Create a meeting as BUYER (expect 403 — staff only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "agency_id": 1, "title": "Reunion equipe", "start_at": "2026-12-01T09:00:00Z", "end_at": "2026-12-01T10:00:00Z" }

### 59. Create a meeting as DIRECTOR with the agent as participant (expect 201)
# @name createMeeting
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

{
  "agency_id": 1,
  "title": "Point hebdo agence",
  "description": "Suivi des dossiers en cours",
  "start_at": "2026-12-01T09:00:00Z",
  "end_at": "2026-12-01T10:00:00Z",
  "location": "Salle A",
  "participant_ids": [1]
}

### 60. Create with end BEFORE start (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

{ "agency_id": 1, "title": "Horaire invalide", "start_at": "2026-12-01T10:00:00Z", "end_at": "2026-12-01T09:00:00Z" }

### 61. Create with a PAST start (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

{ "agency_id": 1, "title": "Dans le passe", "start_at": "2020-01-01T09:00:00Z", "end_at": "2020-01-01T10:00:00Z" }

### 62. Director lists their meetings (expect the meeting, with participants)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

### 63. Agent (a participant) lists their meetings (expect the same meeting)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 64. Agent (not the organizer) tries to delete it (expect 403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings/{{createMeeting.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 65. Director (organizer) deletes it (expect 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings/{{createMeeting.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

### 66. Delete a non-existing meeting (expect 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meetings/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

### =====================================================================
### ALERTS — saved searches (any authenticated user)
### =====================================================================

### 67. Create an alert WITHOUT token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "city": "Paris", "max_price": 500000 }

### 68. Buyer creates an alert (expect 201) — captures the alert id
# @name createAlert
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "city": "Paris", "category_id": 2, "min_price": 200000, "max_price": 500000, "max_energy": "D" }

### 69. Create an alert with an invalid energy class (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "city": "Lyon", "max_energy": "Z" }

### 70. Buyer lists their alerts (expect the alert)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 71. Agent (not the owner) tries to delete the buyer's alert (expect 403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/{{createAlert.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 72. Buyer (owner) deletes their alert (expect 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/{{createAlert.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 73. Delete a non-existing alert (expect 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### =====================================================================
### SALE FILES — agent opens & advances, participants read
### (buyer = user 3, agent = user 1, director = user 2)
### =====================================================================

### 74. Create a sale WITHOUT token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json

{ "property_id": 1, "buyer_id": 3 }

### 75. Create a sale as BUYER (expect 403 — staff only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

{ "property_id": 1, "buyer_id": 3 }

### 76. Create a sale as AGENT (expect 201) — captures the sale id
# @name createSale
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "property_id": 1, "buyer_id": 3, "negotiated_price": 460000, "offer_date": "2026-06-15T00:00:00Z" }

### 77. Create with a missing property (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "property_id": 9999, "buyer_id": 3 }

### 78. Create with a missing buyer (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "property_id": 1, "buyer_id": 9999 }

### 79. Buyer (participant) reads the sale (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales/{{createSale.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBuyer.response.body.token}}

### 80. Director (not a participant) reads it (expect 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales/{{createSale.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

### 81. Director (staff, but not the sale's agent) tries to advance it (expect 403)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales/{{createSale.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginDirector.response.body.token}}

{ "status": "PRELIMINARY_CONTRACT" }

### 82. Agent advances the sale to "compromis" (expect 200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales/{{createSale.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "status": "PRELIMINARY_CONTRACT", "contract_date": "2026-07-01T00:00:00Z" }

### 83. Agent completes the sale (expect 200) — property becomes SOLD
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sales/{{createSale.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "status": "COMPLETED", "deed_date": "2026-09-01T00:00:00Z" }

### 84. The linked property is now SOLD (check status — and it leaves the public catalogue)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/properties/1
